# Dashboard Design System

Simple systems make support dashboards feel effortless. Keep UI minimal, consistent, and scannable.

## Typography

- **Font**: Inter — `font-normal` (400) for body, `font-medium` (500) for emphasis and labels
- **Letter spacing**: `-0.15px` on all text (`tracking-[-0.15px]`)
- **Allowed sizes only**: `12px`, `13px`, `14px`, `24px` — no other font sizes in dashboard UI

| Context | Size | Weight |
|---------|------|--------|
| Sidebar | 12px | regular / medium |
| Main screen | 14px | regular / medium |
| Page titles / primary headings | 24px | medium |
| Secondary labels, metadata | 13px | regular |

Build hierarchy with size and weight — not extra colors or decoration.

## Color

Use only these three text/surface tokens:

| Token | Hex | Use |
|-------|-----|-----|
| Primary text | `#181818` | Body copy, default labels |
| Emphasis | `#141414` | Headings, active nav, strong hierarchy |
| On dark / inverse | `#FFFFFF` | Text on dark surfaces |

```tsx
// ✅ GOOD
<p className="text-sm text-[#181818] tracking-[-0.15px]">Status</p>
<h1 className="text-2xl font-medium text-[#141414] tracking-[-0.15px]">Overview</h1>

// ❌ BAD — arbitrary size or gray scale
<p className="text-[11px] text-gray-500">Status</p>
```

Extend `tailwind.config.ts` with named tokens (`text-primary`, `text-emphasis`) instead of repeating hex values once the config exists.

## Icons

- **Size**: `26px` (`size-[26px]` or `h-[26px] w-[26px]`) everywhere — sidebar nav and main screen actions
- Keep stroke weight consistent; do not mix 16px, 20px, or 32px icons in dashboard surfaces

## Layout rhythm

- Sidebar content uses **12px** type; main content area uses **14px** type
- Do not shrink sidebar copy below 12px or inflate main body above 14px except 24px headings

## Never do

- Add font sizes outside 12 / 13 / 14 / 24
- Use gray-* Tailwind defaults instead of `#181818` / `#141414`
- Size icons differently in sidebar vs main screen
- Stack competing visual cues (color + bold + underline) — pick one hierarchy signal
